<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lough Erne</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lough Erne is a pair of connected lakes on the River Erne in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-fermanagh">County Fermanagh</a>, Northern Ireland. Ptolemy's Erdini are usually placed around it. In the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> its islands and shores formed the heart of the Maguire lordship of Fermanagh, with monasteries such as Devenish and the castle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enniskillen">Enniskillen</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lough-erne.jpg" alt="Lough Erne" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sam2453 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Loch_Erne.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
